cff-version: 1.2.0
title: standseg
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper
  describing the algorithm it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Elaine
    family-names: Ye
repository-code: https://github.com/Sugarc0de/standseg
abstract: >-
  A Rust implementation of the multi-resolution forest stand segmentation
  algorithm of Ye et al. (2025), which extends the Harward & Woodcock (1992)
  nested-hierarchical region-growing segmenter to develop micro-segments against
  a second data layer. Reproduces the original C byte for byte on one image, and
  the reference Python implementation byte for byte on two.
keywords:
  - image segmentation
  - remote sensing
  - forest stand delineation
  - Landsat
  - region growing
license: MIT
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    A multi-resolution forest stand segmentation algorithm integrating Landsat
    imagery and forest structural, age, and species attributes
  authors:
    - given-names: Elaine
      family-names: Ye
    - given-names: Nicholas C.
      family-names: Coops
    - given-names: Michael A.
      family-names: Wulder
    - given-names: Txomin
      family-names: Hermosilla
  journal: ISPRS Journal of Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing
  year: 2025
  doi: 10.1016/j.isprsjprs.2025.05.023
references:
  - type: article
    title: Nested-hierarchical scene models and image segmentation
    authors:
      - given-names: Curtis
        family-names: Woodcock
      - given-names: V. Jud
        family-names: Harward
    journal: International Journal of Remote Sensing
    volume: 13
    issue: 16
    start: 3167
    end: 3187
    year: 1992
